# Same format as manifest/update-notes.psv.
nerdctl|Must stay compatible with the containerd it talks to; check the container runtime version before upgrading.
talosctl|Keep within the supported version skew of your Talos clusters; upgrading ahead of the cluster can use newer API fields.
kubectl|Supported skew is one minor version either side of the cluster's API server; do not move ahead of your clusters blindly.
kubectl-minor|Moves the pinned Kubernetes apt repo to a new minor; check cluster version skew first. Needs apt-repos.sh edit (K8S_MINOR) and a sudo rerun; the Kubernetes key fingerprint is not pinned.
terraform|State files and provider locks can be upgraded irreversibly by a newer Terraform; teammates on older versions may then be unable to use the state. Check required_version constraints.
vault|CLI/server version skew can matter; check the server version you talk to before upgrading.
